{{also|bling-bling}}
==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From Jamaican slang, a sound suggested by the quality of light reflected by diamonds, adopted by American rappers. Compare words of similar sound and meaning: {{m|en|blink}}, {{m|en|blinding}}, {{m|en|blank}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/blɪŋ blɪŋ/}}
* {{audio|en|En-au-bling bling.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# {{lb|en|slang}} [[shiny|Shiny]] [[jewelry]] that displays [[wealth]], such as a [[diamond ring]] or a [[stylish]] [[gold]] [[necklace]] or [[bracelet]].
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.theatlantic.com/national/archive/2014/02/the-rise-of-the-man-gagement-ring/283827/|title=The Rise of the Man-gagement Ring|work=The Atlantic|date=2014-02-14|author=Samantha Zabell|passage=Gay men often seek out diamonds, and some purchases are “'''bling bling''',” according to Jillian Rebol, the manager of Ultra Diamonds (soon to be Kay Jeweler’s) in Chicago.}}

